    body: "Daily carbohydrate is set by the day's training, not by a fixed diet: 3–5 g per kg body weight on rest or very light days, 5–7 g/kg for about an hour of training, 6–10 g/kg for 1–3 hours, 8–12 g/kg for 4–5 hours. Low-carbohydrate approaches lower exercise economy and impair high-intensity performance; they are not used in this plan. Protein 1.6–2.0 g/kg per day in 3–4 portions. Fat makes up the rest, at least 20 % of calories. Velocity's daily targets follow these bands from your weight and the day's sessions.",
