    body: "Sweat rates range from 0.5 to over 2 litres an hour; a sweat-rate test (weigh before and after a one-hour session, add what you drank) gives your number. Aim to lose no more than 2–3 % of body weight in a long session; drinking to thirst is adequate for most sessions under 2 hours, and a plan is needed beyond that. Over-drinking plain water for hours is the dangerous direction (low blood sodium). Sodium 300–1,000 mg per litre of fluid, more for salty sweaters, and 500–1,500 mg/h for a hot long-course race.",
