    body: "One to two days at 10–12 g/kg of carbohydrate with reduced training fills muscle glycogen fully; the old week-long depletion phase is unnecessary. Expect 1–2 kg of extra weight (water stored with glycogen). Keep fibre and fat low from two days out, and eat the race breakfast (2–3 g/kg, 3 hours before) exactly as practised before long sessions. Loading matters for events over 90 minutes; for a 10K it changes little.",
