    id: "energy-availability", title: "Energy availability and weight loss during training", topic: "nutrition", grade: "A",
    tags: ["weight loss", "lose weight", "race weight", "calorie deficit", "red-s", "energy availability", "underfuelling", "lean", "body fat"],
    body: "Energy availability = calories eaten minus calories spent in training, per kg of fat-free mass. Below about 30 kcal/kg FFM per day, hormones, bone, immunity and recovery break down within weeks, in men as well as women; performance falls even when weight does. Weight loss during a training plan is done in base, not build or peak, at a deficit of no more than 250–500 kcal a day, with protein raised to about 2 g/kg, and never on long-session days. Velocity's staged weight targets follow those rules and the app refuses targets that would push energy availability below the floor.",
