    tags: ["drafting", "draft zone", "penalty", "12 metres", "passing", "rules", "blue card"],
    body: "In IRONMAN age-group racing the draft zone is 12 metres from the front wheel of the rider ahead; you may enter it only to pass and must complete the pass within 25 seconds; the passed rider must drop back out of the zone before trying to re-pass. Drafting penalty is a 5-minute stop at the next penalty tent (blue card) for full distance; three draft penalties mean disqualification. Ride on the right unless passing. Littering outside aid stations carries a penalty. Rules differ by federation and race, so read the athlete guide of your race.",
    source: "IRONMAN competition rules (current edition)",
