    body: "A half-distance race 6–10 weeks before a full-distance race rehearses transitions, pacing and fuelling under race stress, which training cannot. It costs about a week: 2 easy days before, 3–4 easy days after. Closer than 5 weeks, the recovery eats into the last build weeks; further than 12, it tells little. Race it at planned full-distance effort on the bike (not all-out) and only the run at half-distance race effort. A 10K or sprint triathlon fits anywhere in build as a hard session with a day of recovery.",
