    body: "Heavy legs on the morning of a quality session are common and usually mean the previous day was harder than planned, sleep was short, or fuelling was low. The rule: warm up for 15 minutes as planned. If the legs come round, do the session. If pace or power in the first interval is more than 5 % below target at the planned heart rate or effort, stop the intervals, finish the time easy, and move the quality session to the next day the plan has free; do not stack it onto another hard day. Two heavy-legged quality sessions in a row, or a resting heart rate 5+ above normal, means the week needs a recovery day, not a rearrangement.",
