    id: "when-to-skip", title: "When to skip a session, when not to", topic: "training", grade: "C",
    tags: ["skip", "miss", "rest day", "should i train", "don't feel like", "motivation", "unplanned rest", "tired", "sick"],
    body: "Skip: fever or below-the-neck illness; sharp or localised pain that changes how you move; less than 5 hours' sleep two nights running; resting heart rate 10+ above normal. Do a shortened easy version instead of skipping: ordinary tiredness, a busy day, a bad mood, light soreness, rain. Do the session as planned: everything else. A skipped session is dropped, not made up. Two skips in a week for the same reason are a planning problem (sessions at the wrong time of day, too much volume for the week's life load), and the fix is the plan, not more willpower.",
